=== layout: two-panels

# 2. What counts as a different microbe?

@left

## The older figures

*OTUs* group similar sequences using a chosen cutoff, often 97%. That cutoff is a convention, not a universal species boundary.

@right

## Another approach

*ASVs* are inferred exact amplicon sequence variants after error correction. DADA2 can distinguish single-base differences. An ASV is still not automatically a species.

@notes

