=== layout: four-panels

# 5. Follow the chlorine

@top-left

## TCE

Trichloroethene: three chlorine atoms. Reduction removes chlorine step by step.

@top-right

## DCE

Dichloroethene: two chlorine atoms. Which isomer and which organism matter.

@bottom-left

## Vinyl chloride

One chlorine atom. A toxic intermediate can accumulate if the pathway stalls.

@bottom-right

## Ethene

No chlorine. Measure the end product before calling the treatment complete.

@notes

2026 topic 5; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
Prompt source: ../old/Fall_2026_Talking_Points_Set_4-Environmental_and_Synthetic.pptx, slide 22.
