2026 topic 9. Instructor-authored concept check.

=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 10: Fuel cells

@body

- Can we collect some of the electrons released when microbes eat?
- At the *anode*, fuel is oxidized. Electrons travel through the external circuit to the *cathode*.
- In a microbial fuel cell, microbes oxidize organic material and transfer electrons toward the anode.
- A fuel cell needs a continuing fuel supply. A battery stores energy in its materials.

@notes

