=== layout: one-panel

# 11. Does the whole system help?

@body

- Algae and cyanobacteria can release oxygen during photosynthesis. CO2 fixation by a chemoautotroph does not automatically make oxygen.
- Could a methanotroph and a photosynthetic partner share gas streams? Include mixing, light, and energy costs.
- Compare biofilters, microbial fuel cells, carbonate precipitation, and soil-carbon stabilization.
- Biochar is made by heating biomass with limited oxygen. Microbes affect its later behavior; they do not make biochar by ordinary growth.

@notes

