# Topic 12: Plastic enzymes

@body

- Plastic is not one chemical. An enzyme that attacks PET does not automatically attack polyethylene.
- Ideonella sakaiensis helped make *PETase* and *MHETase* famous.
- PETase cuts ester bonds in PET; MHETase processes the soluble MHET product.
- The useful question is how much polymer becomes recoverable molecules, under what conditions.

@notes

2026 topic 12; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
Prompt source: ../old/Fall_2026_Talking_Points_Set_4-Environmental_and_Synthetic.pptx, slide 36.
Expanded instructor explanation and discussion, retaining the source questions. Historical student contributions are teaching leads, not scientific authority.
